# Build context is the whole repo (the Maven aggregator needs every module dir), so
# trimming it matters: the raw tree is ~1.4 GB, of which */target alone is ~1.0 GB.
# Everything below is either rebuilt inside the image or must never enter the build.

.git
.gitignore

# Maven output — rebuilt in the build stage. Stale jars here could otherwise shadow a
# fresh build.
**/target

# Frontend has its own build context (frontend/.dockerignore); excluded here so the
# Java build context stays small.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/build

# Python service — not part of any Java image (see Planning_CICD.md Phụ lục A)
ai-service/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# SECRETS + config drift. Every module inherits spring-dotenv, so a leaked .env inside
# the image would silently fill in any variable we forget to declare in compose/Helm
# (root .env currently holds BOOKING_HOLD_MINUTES=1, a leftover QA value) — and it
# carries real Cloudinary / Gemini / LangSmith keys.
.env
.env.*

# Not needed to build
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
*.md
.claude
.idea
.vscode
scripts
**/*.log
.DS_Store
